@flexiarg operator/report-the-operator-side-action
@title Report the Operator-Side Action as Done
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-EvJZPG turn-RY0rPh; first proposed for: A change requires action on both sides (agent code, operator configuration).
@why [agent/evidence-over-assertion]

! conclusion: Report the operator-side state change in one clause when it is a prerequisite or context for what is being discussed.

  + IF:
    The operator has just performed their side (ticked the always-listening button).

  + HOWEVER:
    If only agent actions are reported, the operator's side is invisible and the agent may wait or re-ask for something already done; but narrating every click is noise.

  + THEN:
    Report the operator-side state change in one clause when it is a prerequisite or context for what is being discussed.

  + BECAUSE:
    Evidence-over-assertion wants claims backed by checkable state; the operator-side report is the reverse direction — the human's action enters the shared record as a fact the agent can rely on, symmetric with what agents owe.
